sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor U as User
    participant O as Orchestrator (code)
    participant V as Validator
    participant SB as Sandbox MCP
    participant C as Stage Coder
    participant W as Warehouse MCP

    O->>V: propose(plan, output profiles, raw profiles)
    V-->>O: derived rules (fixed after round 1: no moving goalposts)
    O->>O: add schema rules (dtype, NOT NULL, PK unique, rows > 0) + request rules
    O->>SB: run_quality(datasets, rules)
    SB-->>O: CheckResults
    alt failures and quality_round < max_quality_rounds
        O->>O: producer = first stage (topological) whose dataset failed
        O->>C: write(stage, feedback = failing checks + example rows)
        Note over O,C: then rebuild the producer and every downstream stage
    else no failures, or rounds exhausted (failures shown to the human)
        O->>W: stage_table(final dataset) -> staging__table + fingerprint
        O->>W: write_quarantine(all quarantined rows with reasons)
        O-->>U: interrupt: rows, existing rows, quarantine, failed checks, preview
        Note over O: LangGraph interrupt + SQLite checkpoint: the run waits here
        U->>O: approve (name, note)
        O->>O: token = HMAC(secret, run_id, table, fingerprint)
        O->>W: promote(table, token)
        W->>W: verify token against the STAGED data, then one transaction
        W-->>O: rows loaded
    end
